le. =20
The second says that those referents collectively are not white.  Except wh=
en=20
there is only one referent, it is not perfectly clear what the referents be=
ing=20
(or not being) collectively white means.  On one notion of participation, t=
his=20
would simply make no sense, or, at least, would be categorically false, and=
 so=20
